// Four equal bars on a 3:5 field.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Unlabeled flag"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20220217001658/https://twitter.com/okumura_eijii/status/1337426136658219008"
  source "https://lgbtqia.fandom.com/wiki/Unlabeled"
  note "The designer and first publication were not found. The earliest source read is a tweet of 11 December 2020 (Wayback Machine, 17 February 2022), whose author doesn't claim the design: 'hey. hi. this is the unlabelled pride flag. it's not very well known but it exists'. Its image labels the stripes freedom, understanding, acceptance and flexibility, the meanings the LGBTQIA+ Wiki (Fandom) also gives."
  note "Colors are the medians of each stripe's unlettered part in that tweet's image (1200 by 641 JPEG), which is not the designer's: #dcfde0, #fdfef6, #d8f0fa, #fee0bc. The image is lossy, so these are approximate. Its stripes are uneven, about 146, 168, 170 and 157 pixels, and are taken as equal. The 3:5 proportion is the common one, not from a source."
}
palette {
  green "#dcfde0"
  white "#fdfef6"
  blue "#d8f0fa"
  orange "#fee0bc"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars green white blue orange
